error[SC0411]: this reads a pointer out of memory before anything was assigned to it
   ╭─[ a_copy_out_of_a_block_nothing_wrote_into_a_local_array_is_reported_where_read.c:2:89 ]
   │
 2 │ int f(int *x) { int **m = malloc(8); if (!m) return 0; int *a[1]; memcpy(a, m, 8); int *r = a[0]; return r == x; }
   │                                                                   ───────┬───────       ────┬───  
   │                                                                          ╰──────────────────────── the bytes were copied here from `m`
   │                                                                                             │     
   │                                                                                             ╰───── read here
───╯
  = note: C17 7.24.2.1 to 7.24.3.1 copy the source's characters into the destination, so bytes nothing wrote there are indeterminate where they land, and Annex J.2 lists using that value as undefined
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = help: write what the copy reads before copying it
